    "result_text": "The full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS, 0 failures). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `initials` field on the Owner response:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` property to the `Owner` schema (alongside the existing `displayName`), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` for `initials` using the same expression pattern as `displayName`:\n   ```java\n   Character.toUpperCase(owner.getFirstName().charAt(0)) + \".\" +\n   Character.toUpperCase(owner.getLastName().charAt(0)) + \".\"\n   ```\n   This upper-cases the first letters of firstName and lastName, dot-separates them with a trailing dot, so `firstName=john, lastName=smith` \u2192 `\"J.S.\"`.\n\nThe `GET /api/owners/{ownerId}` pipeline already responds via `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, so no endpoint wiring changes were needed. `AcceptanceTest.coreComputesInitials` and the full test suite pass.",
